                <pb facs="0825" n="709" sameAs="frus:frus1923v01/pg709"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1123 Coltman, Charles/–: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Schurman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-12-12T16:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 12,
                                1922—4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received December 12—11:22
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>489. Charles Coltman, American merchant, was shot by Chinese soldiers in Kalgan,
                    afternoon 11th, after dispute as to his right to <pb facs="0826" n="710"
                        xml:id="pg710"/> leave Kalgan in automobile with silver currency. Spinal
                    cord injured. May possibly live but paralyzed. Receiving best medical treatment
                    Peking. Report follows.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Schurman</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
